WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.050
20 badges take you from the simulators
to flying at school events.

2
00:00:05.533 --> 00:00:08.373
Every badge has a card on the Pilot Path.

3
00:00:08.413 --> 00:00:10.853
Most have a short video, then a quiz.

4
00:00:10.893 --> 00:00:13.933
80% passes, and retakes are free.

5
00:00:13.973 --> 00:00:16.743
Pass a quiz-only badge, and it's yours.

6
00:00:17.233 --> 00:00:22.553
Hands-on badges, like Soldering, Building
and Betaflight, come with instructions.

7
00:00:22.593 --> 00:00:26.923
Follow the steps, submit a photo
of your work, and a mentor checks it.

8
00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:29.840
Flight badges end in a checkride.

9
00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:32.080
A mentor watches it in person.

10
00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:37.490
Sim Flight is different: you record it
on a sim, and a mentor passes it online.

11
00:00:37.967 --> 00:00:39.767
Badges come in tiers.

12
00:00:39.807 --> 00:00:44.087
Each tier ends in a checkpoint,
a test flight that's also a badge.

13
00:00:44.127 --> 00:00:48.007
Five badges lead
to the Meteor 75 Pro Certification.

14
00:00:48.047 --> 00:00:50.087
Pass it and you're Tier 1.

15
00:00:50.127 --> 00:00:53.127
Six more lead to the Pavo 20 Pro Flight.

16
00:00:53.167 --> 00:00:55.527
Tier 2 means bigger drones.

17
00:00:55.567 --> 00:00:58.857
Six more lead to Event Pilot, Tier 3.

18
00:00:59.333 --> 00:01:02.893
To become an Event Pilot,
you need everything before it.

19
00:01:02.933 --> 00:01:05.173
Every badge, every checkpoint.

20
00:01:05.213 --> 00:01:06.253
No skipping.

21
00:01:06.293 --> 00:01:09.983
A checkpoint opens once
every badge in its tier is done.

22
00:01:10.733 --> 00:01:13.893
Already fly, or already solder?

23
00:01:13.933 --> 00:01:16.053
Your past experience counts.

24
00:01:16.093 --> 00:01:19.973
Show a mentor what you can do,
and they can check those badges off.

25
00:01:20.013 --> 00:01:22.103
You don't start from zero.

26
00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:25.820
Passing a checkpoint
doesn't clear you to fly.

27
00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:28.620
Flight Clearance does, on its own page.

28
00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:29.420
New here?

29
00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:32.140
Scan the code on a sim
screen to add your name.

30
00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:35.310
Then pick it on the Pilot Path
and press play.

